PATCH 113: reconstruct MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_0f62 (2nd-element background-SAVE blit).

0f62 (asm 0xf62..0xfbb) is the element background-SAVE blit: es:0 (save buffer) <- ds:si (framebuffer
rect).  di=dx=param_1 = the SAVE descriptor (DGROUP near off); bx=param_2 = the RECT descriptor.  Three
Ghidra defects, all asm-verified:
  (a) param_1/param_2 were typed as HOST pointers (`param_1+1`, `*param_2`), but they are DGROUP near
      offsets -- rebase to g_mem+0x1c000+off (this is what SEGV'd once di was threaded to 0xf6ee: the
      code deref'd host address 0xf6ee+2).
  (b) the ES (save-buffer seg = save.w0), DS (framebuffer seg = word[[0x724]]) and DGROUP row-table base
      [0x794] rep-movs bases were all dropped (the copy started at host NULL).
  (c) the EARLY-RETURN idiom `jns 0xf77 ; call 0xf60` was mis-modeled: 0f60 = `pop ax; ret` pops the
      return-into-0f62 address and FAR-RETURNS to 0f62's caller (an early return), but Ghidra rendered it
      as a normal call and then blit unconditionally through the NULL es.
Reconstruct faithfully: `or byte[di+2],0x20; jns -> return; test 0x10 -> 2c8b; blit`.  For the MAINMENU
2nd element the descriptor flag byte starts 0 => after |0x20 the sign bit is clear => EARLY RETURN, so no
save buffer is touched on first paint (the reserve method 0f1a's [DGROUP:0xcc] object-vtable slot is not
resident this phase; the blit path is only taken when the element is marked dirty, sign bit set).  The
signature changes from (undefined2*,int*) to (undefined2,undefined2) to carry the two DGROUP offsets.
Asm-verified 0xf62..0xfbb (and 0xf60 the pop/ret early-return trampoline).
